cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Conditional Continuation and Small-Data Regularity for 3D Navier–Stokes on T³, with the Frohmanian Symplectic Tether as a Metric (Non-Poisson) Correction"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Frohman
    given-names: Benjamin Stanley
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-7068-3718"
    email: frohmanbenjamin@gmail.com
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/BenFrohman/frohmanian-tether-conditional-regularity"
keywords:
  - Navier-Stokes
  - Beale-Kato-Majda
  - Kozono-Taniuchi
  - Kato local existence
  - Fujita-Kato
  - metriplectic
  - Frohmanian Symplectic Tether
abstract: >-
  Expository, conditional preprint. Theorems A (Beale–Kato–Majda /
  Kozono–Taniuchi continuation criterion), B (Kato local existence) and
  C (Fujita–Kato small-data global existence) are classical results, cited
  as such. The Frohmanian Symplectic Tether B(F,G) is symmetric and is
  treated as a metric-type (metriplectic) term, not a Poisson correction.
  Large-data global regularity remains open; no Clay Millennium Problem
  proof is claimed. The paper is licensed CC-BY-4.0; code is Apache-2.0.
